sections.raw_text:
A Pradeshiya Sabha may, within its limits either independently or in
conjunction with any other local authority or any other person,
establish and maintain for the benefit of the persons inhabiting or
resorting to such area, the following public utility services:
(a) water supply;
(b) the lighting of streets, public places and public: buildings;
(c) the supply of electricity or power;
(d) markets;
(e) rest houses;
(f) public baths and bathing places;
(g) the manufacture and supply at cost price of squatting plates
for latrines;
(h) the provision of housing accommodation for the poorer
classes;
(i) any other form of public service which the Pradeshiya Sabha
is authorized to establish, maintain or provide under any other
provision of this Act, or under any other written law.

